.TH ASK 1 2026-11-07 "agent-kit" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ask, ask-codex, ask-claude, ask-agy, ask-opencode \- send one prompt to a coding agent CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ask
.RI [ options ]
.I tool model
.RI [ prompt ...]
.br
.B ask-codex
.RI [ options ]
.I model
.RI [ prompt ...]
.br
.B ask-claude
.RI [ options ]
.I model
.RI [ prompt ...]
.br
.B ask-agy
.RI [ options ]
.I model
.RI [ prompt ...]
.br
.B ask-opencode
.RI [ options ]
.I model
.RI [ prompt ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ask
sends one prompt to a coding agent CLI and prints the tool's final message
on stdout.
Every tool gets the same command line and the same exit codes.
.PP
.I tool
is one of
.BR codex ,
.BR claude ,
.B agy
or
.BR opencode .
Started as
.BI ask\- tool\fR,
through a symlink to
.BR ask ,
the tool comes from the program name and the model is the first word.
Only those four names count.
.PP
The prompt is the words after the model, joined with spaces.
A lone
.B \-
adds stdin to the prompt.
Without it,
.B ask
never reads stdin.
Each
.B \-f
file is added after that, starting with a line
.BI "\-\-\- " name " \-\-\-" .
A
.B \-f
path is relative to the folder
.B ask
starts in, not the
.B \-C
folder.
The parts are joined with a blank line.
An empty prompt is an error.
.PP
Flags may appear anywhere on the line.
A
.B \-\-
ends the flags, so every word after it is prompt text.
.PP
The prompt never goes on the tool's command line.
claude and codex read it from stdin.
For agy and opencode,
.B ask
writes it to a temp file (folder mode 0700, file mode 0600) and removes
the folder when the run ends.
agy gets the instruction
.RI \(dq "Read the file <path> and follow the instructions in it." \(dq
opencode gets the file with
.BI \-f " path"
and the instruction
.RI \(dq "Follow the instructions in the attached file." \(dq
Prompt words typed as arguments do show in
.BR ask 's
own command line, which other users can see with
.BR ps (1).
Use
.B \-
or
.B \-f
for private text.
.PP
Read\-only is the default.
Without
.BR \-\-write ,
.B ask
runs a tool only if its read\-only setup passed its test on the installed
version, compared with the trimmed output of
.IB tool " \-\-version" .
Otherwise it refuses with exit 2.
A read\-only run gets only the secrets listed in
.BR read_only_secrets ,
and runs once more if the tool exits non\-zero with no final message.
A
.B \-\-write
run gets every configured secret and never retries.
.PP
.B ask
never runs a tool's login command.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-write
Let the tool edit files and run MCP servers and hooks.
.TP
.BI \-C " folder" "\fR, \fP\-\-dir " folder
Run the tool in this folder.
The default is the current folder.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " duration"
Stop the tool after this long, as a Go duration such as
.BR 90s ,
.B 5m
or
.BR 1h30m .
The default is the tool's
.B timeout_seconds
from the config, or 10 minutes.
.B 0
means the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-effort " level"
Reasoning effort.
claude and agy take
.BR low ,
.BR medium ,
.BR high ,
.B xhigh
or
.BR max .
codex and opencode take none, and
.B ask
refuses the flag for them.
.TP
.BI \-\-final " regex"
Print only the last line of the final message that matches the Go regular
expression, then the report path.
Exit 1 when no line matches.
Cannot be used with
.BR \-\-no\-report .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show the command
.B ask
would start, as one line, and run nothing.
The line is for reading, not for running.
A secret shows as
.IB ENV_VAR =< key >\fR,
never its value.
The prompt shows as
.BI <prompt: " N " bytes>
or, for agy and opencode,
.BI <prompt: " N " "bytes, in a temp file>"\fR;
that temp file is removed before
.B ask
exits.
A dry run looks up no secrets, runs no version check, saves no report and
writes no log line.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-report
Do not save the final message to a report file.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
After a run that started the tool, print one summary line on stderr.
A refusal, bad arguments or a setup failure print only the error.
The line has this shape:
.RS
.PP
.nf
ask: tool=\fItool\fP model=\fImodel\fP model_id=\fIid\fP
     reported_model=\fIname\fP duration=\fId\fP tokens=\fIin\fP/\fIout\fP
     exit=\fIcode\fP report=\fIpath\fP
.fi
.RE
.IP
The real line has no breaks.
.B model_id
is the model passed to the tool after the config short\-name lookup.
.B reported_model
is the model the tool says it used, or
.B none
when it names none; only claude names one today.
.B report=none
means no report was saved.
After a failed run, also print the last 4 KiB of the tool's stderr, with
secrets redacted.
.TP
.BI \-f " file" "\fR, \fP\-\-file " file
Add a file's text to the prompt.
Repeat for more files.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the help text.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.B claude
Read\-only runs only on version
.BR "2.1.319 (Claude Code)" ,
with the Read, Grep and Glob tools and no hooks, MCP servers or user
settings.
After an upgrade, read\-only is refused until the new version is tested.
With
.BR \-\-write ,
claude runs with
.B "\-\-permission\-mode acceptEdits"
and without
.BR \-\-safe\-mode ,
so user settings load and hooks and MCP servers are not turned off.
Model aliases such as
.B haiku
mean whatever the installed claude maps them to; give a full model ID to
pin one.
.TP
.B codex
Read\-only is refused; its test was inconclusive.
With
.BR \-\-write ,
codex runs in the
.B workspace\-write
sandbox.
.TP
.B agy
Read\-only is refused; it is not tested.
With
.BR \-\-write ,
agy runs with
.BR "\-\-mode accept\-edits" .
.TP
.B opencode
Read\-only is refused; it has no read\-only setup.
With
.BR \-\-write ,
.B opencode run
runs with
.BR \-\-auto .
Models are
.IB provider / model
IDs.
.PP
A tool's
.B models
map in the config turns a short name into a full model name.
A name not in the map passes through as typed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
ok
.TP
.B 1
The tool failed, gave no final message, or
.B \-\-final
found no match.
.TP
.B 2
Bad arguments, or
.B ask
refused the run.
.TP
.B 3
.BR ask 's
own setup failed: config, secret lookup, missing binary or report save.
.TP
.B 124
Timeout.
.TP
.BI 128+ n
The tool or
.B ask
was killed by signal
.IR n .
.PP
On a timeout or a signal,
.B ask
stops the tool's whole process group.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base of the config path.
Used only when it is an absolute path.
.TP
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
Base of the state folder for reports and the log.
Used only when it is an absolute path.
.TP
.B HOME
Used when the XDG variables are unset.
.PP
The tool does not inherit
.BR ask 's
whole environment.
It gets
.BR PATH ,
.BR HOME ,
.BR USER ,
.BR LANG ,
.BR TERM ,
.BR TMPDIR ,
.BR SHELL ,
every
.B XDG_*
variable, the variables named in the config's
.BR pass_env ,
and the secrets for this mode, each in its
.BR env_var .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/agent\-kit/config.json
The config file, or
.I ~/.config/agent\-kit/config.json
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset.
It holds per\-tool
.BR binary ,
.BR models ,
.BR timeout_seconds ,
.BR secrets ,
.B read_only_secrets
and
.BR pass_env ,
and a top\-level
.BR report_days .
It never holds a secret value.
A secret's
.B ref
is
.BI keychain: account @ service
(macOS only),
.BI env: NAME\fR,
.BI file: path
or
.BI cmd: command\fR.
Without a config file, each tool is found on PATH and no secrets are
passed.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ask/reports/
Report files, or
.I ~/.local/state/ask/reports/
when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is unset.
Each is named
.IB time \- tool \- pid \- n .md\fR,
holds the final message with secrets redacted, and has mode 0600.
Reports older than
.B report_days
(default 30) are deleted.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/ask/log.jsonl
One JSON line per run, mode 0600, with the fields
.BR time ,
.BR tool ,
.BR model ,
.BR model_id ,
.BR reported_model ,
.BR duration_ms ,
.BR exit ,
.B input_tokens
and
.BR output_tokens .
It never holds the prompt.
.SH EXAMPLES
Ask claude, read\-only:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ask claude haiku "What does internal/runner/runner.go do?"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Review a diff sent on stdin:
.PP
.RS
.nf
git diff main | ask\-claude sonnet "Review this diff for bugs." \-
.fi
.RE
.PP
Let codex edit files in another folder:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ask codex my\-model \-\-write \-C ~/src/project \-f task.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Print only the verdict line and the report path:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ask claude haiku \-\-final \(aq^VERDICT:\(aq \-f review\-prompt.md
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show the command without running it:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ask opencode \-\-write \-\-dry\-run ollama/example\-model "Fix the typo."
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send a word that looks like a flag as prompt text:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ask claude haiku \-\- \-\-verbose is a flag name
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ps (1)
.PP
The full guide is
.I docs/ask/README.md
in the agent\-kit repository.
